  'indonesia-pantau-aksi-one-health-amr',
  'Isu Terkini',
  'Indonesia pantau aksi One Health lawan resistensi antimikroba',
  'Indonesia monitors One Health action against antimicrobial resistance',

  'Indonesia ikut survei global TrACSS (WHO, FAO, UNEP, WOAH) untuk mengukur kemajuan perang melawan resistensi antimikroba — lewat pendekatan One Health: manusia, hewan, dan lingkungan.',
  'Indonesia joined the global TrACSS survey (WHO, FAO, UNEP, WOAH) to measure progress against antimicrobial resistance — through a One Health approach: humans, animals, and the environment.',

  '<h4>Ancaman yang bikin obat kalah</h4><p>Resistensi antimikroba (AMR) adalah salah satu ancaman kesehatan paling serius di dunia: infeksi yang tadinya mudah disembuhkan menjadi sulit ditangani, risikonya penyakit lama, disabilitas, bahkan kematian. Bakteri resisten juga bisa berpindah antara <strong>manusia, hewan, dan lingkungan</strong> — jadi lawannya bukan cuma soal dokter dan pasien.</p><h4>Apa itu One Health?</h4><p>Karena mikroba resisten menyebar lintas sektor, cara menghadapinya harus <strong>lintas sektor</strong> juga. Pendekatan One Health memandang kesehatan manusia, hewan, dan lingkungan sebagai satu sistem yang terhubung — dokter hewan, ahli lingkungan, ahli pangan, dan dokter manusia bekerja di <em>meja yang sama</em>.</p><h4>TrACSS — rapor AMR dunia</h4><p>Negara-negara mengikuti <strong>Tracking AMR Country Self-Assessment Survey (TrACSS)</strong>, survei tahunan yang dikoordinasikan WHO, FAO, UNEP, dan WOAH. Hasil TrACSS sebelumnya menjadi dasar <strong>strategi nasional AMR Indonesia 2025-2029</strong> dan membantu menentukan sektor prioritas yang ikut program.</p><h4>Yang dilakukan Indonesia tahun 2026</h4><p>Pada 4-6 Juni 2026, Kementerian Kesehatan bersama WHO menggelar rapat validasi multisektoral untuk pengisian TrACSS 2026: wakil <strong>manusia, hewan, perikanan, pangan-pertanian, dan lingkungan</strong> meninjau bukti sebelum data dikirim. Ketua Tim Kerja AMR dan IPC Kemenkes, Dr Amy Rahmadanti, menyebut TrACSS sebagai kesempatan mengecek kemajuan kolektif Indonesia berbasis bukti. Hasilnya: kuesioner TrACSS 2026 dituntaskan dan dikirim pada <strong>12 Juni 2026</strong>.</p><h4>Kenapa penting bagimu?</h4><p>Diagnosis laboratorium yang mampu mendeteksi bakteri resisten dibangun dari fisikawan lab yang terlatih — seperti pelatihan yang WHO tampilkan di Jakarta. Pemahaman tentang <strong>plasmid dan konjugasi</strong> (cara bakteri tukar gen resistensi) menjelaskan kenapa survei lintas sektor seperti TrACSS begitu krusial: gen resistensi tidak peduli batas antara manusia dan hewan.</p><p>Sumber: WHO Indonesia, <em>Monitoring One Health action against antimicrobial resistance in Indonesia</em> (4 September 2026). <a href="https://www.who.int/indonesia/news/detail/04-09-2026-monitoring-one-health-action-against-antimicrobial-resistance-in-indonesia" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Baca berita aslinya</a>.</p>',

  '<h4>When medicine loses the fight</h4><p>Antimicrobial resistance (AMR) is one of the most serious public health threats in the world: infections that were once easy to cure become hard to treat, raising the risk of prolonged illness, disability, and even death. Resistant microbes can also move between <strong>humans, animals, and the environment</strong> — so this is not only a doctor-patient problem.</p><h4>What is One Health?</h4><p>Because resistant microbes cross-sector lines, the response must be <strong>multisectoral</strong> too. The One Health approach treats human, animal, and environmental health as one connected system — doctors, veterinarians, environmental scientists, and food experts work at the <em>same table</em>.</p><h4>TrACSS — the world''s AMR report card</h4><p>Countries take part in the annual <strong>Tracking AMR Country Self-Assessment Survey (TrACSS)</strong>, coordinated by WHO, FAO, UNEP, and WOAH. Previous TrACSS findings informed <strong>Indonesia''s 2025-2029 national AMR strategy</strong> and helped identify priority sectors and participants for implementation.</p><h4>What Indonesia did in 2026</h4><p>On 4-6 June 2026, the Ministry of Health with WHO support convened a national multisectoral validation meeting for the 2026 TrACSS submission: representatives from <strong>human health, animal health, fisheries, food-agriculture, and the environment</strong> reviewed the evidence before it was submitted. Dr Amy Rahmadanti, Head of the AMR and IPC Working Team at the Ministry of Health, called TrACSS an important opportunity to review Indonesia''s collective progress based on clear evidence. The result: Indonesia finalized and sent its 2026 TrACSS questionnaire on <strong>12 June 2026</strong>.</p><h4>Why does this matter to you?</h4><p>Laboratories able to detect resistant bacteria are staffed by trained technicians — like the AMR training WHO showed in Jakarta. Understanding <strong>plasmids and conjugation</strong> (how bacteria trade resistance genes) explains why a cross-sector survey like TrACSS matters so much: resistance genes do not respect the border between humans and animals.</p><p>Source: WHO Indonesia, <em>Monitoring One Health action against antimicrobial resistance in Indonesia</em> (4 September 2026). <a href="https://www.who.int/indonesia/news/detail/04-09-2026-monitoring-one-health-action-against-antimicrobial-resistance-in-indonesia" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the original article</a>.</p>',

